WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.190
Two in three: 67 per cent.

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:08.990
That was the share of people in East Asia
and Pacific in extreme poverty in 1990.

3
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:14.250
By 2025, on the World Bank's
nowcast: 1.7 per cent.

4
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:20.210
Worldwide, there were about 1.5 billion
fewer people in extreme poverty in 2025

5
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:22.310
than in 1990.

6
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:27.150
Yet in sub-Saharan Africa, the number
of extremely poor people went up.

7
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.050
Why?

8
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.290
A higher poverty line for Africa?

9
00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.470
Asia's poor no longer counted?

10
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.410
In this mission, you'll learn how
the World Bank draws its line:

11
00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.590
3 dollars a person a day.

12
00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:40.870
Then you'll meet the
new global middle class,

13
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.310
and ask how firmly anyone can count it.

14
00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:49.010
Your mission: explain why the number of
extremely poor people in sub-Saharan Africa

15
00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:49.870
rose.
